WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.605
Stage nine: wear and tear.

2
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:12.433
Each session is credited to a pair: the blue Crête Pro, six hundred and twelve kilometres of seven hundred.

3
00:00:12.533 --> 00:00:15.279
Retirement: about two weeks away.

4
00:00:16.129 --> 00:00:20.283
One run pushes the pair past seven hundred kilometres.

5
00:00:20.383 --> 00:00:23.385
The sync adds it to the notification.

6
00:00:23.485 --> 00:00:24.887
Once only.

7
00:00:25.737 --> 00:00:29.976
Every two hundred kilometres, the coach suggests an inspection.

8
00:00:30.076 --> 00:00:33.676
Type /inspection: it asks for five views.

9
00:00:33.776 --> 00:00:38.015
Both soles, profile, heel, upper, and a coin for scale.

10
00:00:38.865 --> 00:00:43.552
The verdict comes in four colours, justified by what the coach sees.

11
00:00:43.652 --> 00:00:48.489
Above all, it compares with the previous inspection: the surest signal.

12
00:00:49.339 --> 00:00:53.024
Worn on the outer heel: a hint of heel strike.

13
00:00:53.124 --> 00:00:54.995
Never a diagnosis.

14
00:00:55.095 --> 00:00:57.457
No coin, no millimetres.

15
00:00:57.557 --> 00:01:00.495
And no stride advice from a photo.

16
00:01:01.345 --> 00:01:05.990
When the watch measures your stride, the measurement wins over the sole.

17
00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:09.753
Balance is a gap from fifty percent, never a foot.

18
00:01:09.853 --> 00:01:12.450
No measurement? The coach says so.

19
00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:19.011
Beyond shoes, the trail kit has its own thresholds: head torch, bladder, poles.

20
00:01:19.111 --> 00:01:21.089
Flagged once at sync.

21
00:01:21.189 --> 00:01:24.405
And before a night run: the head torch battery.

22
00:01:25.255 --> 00:01:28.385
A retired pair gets a career summary.

23
00:01:28.485 --> 00:01:32.298
Distance, sessions, longest run, last inspection.

24
00:01:34.848 --> 00:01:38.917
To go further: the “Shoe inspection” documentation page.
